    "notes": "1. For total_revenue, the primary statement line 'Total revenues and other income' is composed of three sub-items: Sales and other operating revenue, Income from equity affiliates, and Other income. All three are included as they sum to the total. 2. For total_operating_cost, the standard practice for the oil & gas industry includes all costs directly tied to operations before interest and taxes. This includes: cost of goods sold (Crude oil and product purchases), operating expenses (Production and manufacturing, Selling, general and administrative), depreciation/depletion/impairment, exploration costs, pension expense (non-service), and other operating taxes and duties. 'Other taxes and duties' are included as they are operating costs (e.g., production, property, severance taxes) per Note 19. 3. Interest expense is a separate financial cost, not an operating cost. 4. Income tax expense is the tax on income. 5. Net income is the final line attributable to the parent company. 6. All values are taken directly from the primary statement. Supplementary tables provide detail but do not change the totals used. 7. The sign convention for taxes, interest_expenses, and total_operating_cost follows rule 13: values that reduce income are reported as positive numbers. All extracted values are positive as they appear in the statement as deductions.",
